  "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385/assets/7f97a7bd9e722440e1fd7bfe1a7293f989928275cd9b88369aa5650bce1037dd.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,y\\le x\\le 9-2y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{y}^{9-2y}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{y}^{9-2y}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
